      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The enforcement approach is a short-term fix because it's based on a flawed assumption that building more walls and hiring more border agents will magically stop the flow of undocumented immigrants. The data shows that the US-Mexico border has been getting more porous, not less, despite the billions of dollars spent on border security. In fact, a study by the Cato Institute found that for every dollar spent on border security, the US loses an estimated $1.50 in economic growth due to the costs of detaining and deporting undocumented immigrants.",
      "source": "target",
